title: Cooperatives
card-image: img/cards/social_welfare.svg
subtitle: Food networks outside the requisition.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: soviet_affairs
view-if: social_welfare_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; social_welfare_timer = 4

The consumer cooperatives are old, well-managed and run by our friends. They can move food that the state cannot, and the state would like to take them over.

- @expand: Expand cooperative food distribution.
- @credit: Support cooperative credit and the rural cooperatives.
- @defend: Defend the cooperatives against nationalisation.
- @easy_discard

@expand
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bread: 4, repression: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, middle: 3, peasants: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -2);
Q.coops = (Q.coops || 0) + 1;
!}

Cooperative shops reached several cities that the state's food organisations could not. It is the best argument for a market, and everybody knows it.

@credit
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bread: 2, ruble: 2});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 4, middle: 1});
Q.coops = (Q.coops || 0) + 1;
Q.resources += 1;
!}

Rural cooperatives now lend, buy and sell for the peasants. A village that does business through a cooperative learns to expect that it will get paid.

@defend
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {repression: 2, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {middle: 3, workers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -3);
Q.coops = (Q.coops || 0) + 1;
!}

We argued for the cooperatives as free associations of the people. The cooperatives' own leaders were more grateful than the government.
